  "guide": {"focus":"Drawn shapes can have curves, hollows and parts made from different materials. The simulator splits them into convex pieces to check collisions.","predict":{"prompt":"What remains after separating the compound tool?","options":["Separate editable parts","One unchanged body","No objects"]},"variables":[{"control":"object.properties.material","label":"Bracket material","body":"body-1-2"}],"steps":[{"text":"Select the bracket and open Edit shape to inspect its nodes and collision parts.","control":"object.shape.edit","body":"body-1-2"},{"text":"Select the compound tool and use Separate parts.","control":"object.shape.separate","body":"body-3-4"},{"text":"Shift-select two drawn objects and combine them.","control":"object.several.combine"}],"expect":"Apply accepts a valid outline. Separate parts turns the pieces into independent bodies, and Combine joins selected parts into one body.","limits":"Outlines must enclose an area without crossing themselves. Curves are approximated using the selected drawing and collision tolerances."},
